.policy "ruff-n805-invalid-first-argument-name-for-method" revision 2
.description "Use self as the name of the first parameter of instance methods, as PEP 8 recommends."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff N805 (pep8-naming): an instance method whose first positional parameter is not named `self`. A def
// directly in a class body is an instance method unless it is a static or class method (decorators, configurable
// with `pep8-naming.staticmethod-decorators` / `classmethod-decorators`; `__init_subclass__` and
// `__class_getitem__` implicitly), `__new__`, or a method of a metaclass (N804 checks those). Names matching
// `pep8-naming.ignore-names` are exempt.
//   class C:
//       def m(this): ...            ← N805 at `this`
//       @staticmethod
//       def s(x): ...               not reported
#include "python/naming.rr"

.violation N805(at: node, x: symbol) code "N805"
    "Name the first parameter `self` instead of `{x}` and update its uses; if it should receive the class, add `@classmethod` and name it `cls`."
    suppress ruff "N805"
N805(nm, x) :- naming_method_kind(f, "method"), naming_first_param(f, nm, x), x != "self", !naming_ignored(x).
